<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>Downloads the current release of MuseScore Studio for Windows (the 64-bit .msi asset of the newest non-pre-release on GitHub that has a matching file, kept under the asset's own file name) and checks it against the SHA-256 that GitHub records for the asset. When the asset has no recorded digest the run stops with an error and writes nothing: the program is then a hand import until a release with a digest exists. The asset names, sizes and digest flags were read from GitHub's release list on 2026-11-13 (the newest 30 releases): the project names the installer like MuseScore-Studio-&lt;version&gt;-x86_64.msi (the portable .paf.exe beside it is not taken) and has attached it to every release from v4.3.0 on; GitHub records a digest for it from the pre-release v4.6.0-alpha on, so v4.5.2 and older have none; the three oldest releases of the list (v4.2.1 and older) name the file MuseScore-&lt;version&gt;-x86_64.msi, which the pattern does not take. Nothing has run under AutoPkg yet: read the line that names the selected asset and release in the first dry run. AutoPkg takes the first release that has a matching file however old it is, so a release without the MSI would send the recipe back to the newest one that has it. The recipe never stops on an unchanged download, so a failed import is tried again at the next run. Pre-releases are skipped unless the override sets the input include_prereleases to true (three of the 30 releases read are flagged as one: v4.6.0-alpha, v4.6.0-beta and v4.2.0-beta.2; the first two carry an MSI of the same name). The step GitHubNewestReleaseGuard, right after the provider, stops the run when the release that the provider selected is not the newest release (a pre-release is skipped unless include_prereleases is true): it names the newest release and its files. The override's input accepted_newest_release, set to the tag of a newest release that has no Windows installer file (.msi, .exe, .msix) on purpose, lets the run go on only while that release is the newest, and release_tag_pattern names the line of releases to follow for a vendor with two lines (every run names the newer releases that it left out).</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.MuseScore-Win</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>MuseScore</string>
            <key>SEARCH_PATTERN</key>
            <string>MuseScore-Studio-[0-9.]+-x86_64\.msi$</string>
            <key>accepted_newest_release</key>
            <string></string>
            <key>include_prereleases</key>
            <false/>
            <key>release_tag_pattern</key>
            <string></string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>GitHubReleasesInfoProvider</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>github_repo</key>
                    <string>musescore/MuseScore</string>
                    <key>asset_regex</key>
                    <string>%SEARCH_PATTERN%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/GitHubNewestReleaseGuard</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>github_asset_api_url</key>
                    <string>%asset_url%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>URLDownloader</string>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>EndOfCheckPhase</string>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/GitHubAssetDigest</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>github_asset_api_url</key>
                    <string>%asset_url%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/ChecksumVerifier</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                    <key>expected_sha256</key>
                    <string>%expected_sha256%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
